{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1217, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nYou are given an integer array nums and two integers, k and m.\nReturn the maximum sum of k non-overlapping subarrays of nums, where each subarray has a length of at least m.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: nums = [1,2,-1,3,3,4], k = 2, m = 2\nOutput: 13\nExplanation:\nThe optimal choice is:\n\nSubarray nums[3..5] with sum 3 + 3 + 4 = 10 (length is 3 >= m).\nSubarray nums[0..1] with sum 1 + 2 = 3 (length is 2 >= m).\n\nThe total sum is 10 + 3 = 13.\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: nums = [-10,3,-1,-2], k = 4, m = 1\nOutput: -10\nExplanation:\nThe optimal choice is choosing each element as a subarray. The output is (-10) + 3 + (-1) + (-2) = -10.\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n1 <= nums.length <= 2000\n-10^4 <= nums[i] <= 10^4\n1 <= k <= floor(nums.length / m)\n1 <= m <= 3\n\n### Format: You will use the following starter code to write the solution to the problem and enclose your code within delimiters.\n```python\nclass Solution:\n    def maxSum(self, nums: List[int], k: int, m: int) -> int:\n        \n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1270, "char_start": 1229, "quote": "Input:\n[1, 2, -1, 3, 3, 4]\n2\n2\nOutput:\n13", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 1321, "char_start": 1282, "quote": "Input:\n[-10, 3, -1, -2]\n4\n1\nOutput:\n-10", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "dac1d05d10c6f75d0e06d6ef62647f1f6cbc5011874eab822ba3dedfb913ef01", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "b4d36fa9d5924726fb46d5b029e8e76d2f212a32e08e7ce2671d5d1dbf7354c2", "seq": 2}
